IMPORT prelude

-- Limitation of Actions Act 1958 (Vic) -- seat-neutral core.
--
-- Edition: Act No. 6295/1958, Version No. 113, as at 2 October 2026 (includes s 23AB, inserted by No. 45/2026
-- s 18E, in force 2 October 2026, and the Division 5 amendments of No. 5/2026 ss 4-9, in force 25 February 2026),
-- as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/limitation-of-actions-act-1958.txt, a plain-text conversion of the
-- Word file the owner saved by hand on 2026-11-07. Line numbers below are lines of that file.
--
-- Borrowed terms are asked as facts, never worked out here: "dust-related condition" (Administration and Probate
-- Act 1958 s 3(1)); "survivor action" (s 27A, by reference to Administration and Probate Act 1958 s 29); an action
-- that "arises under Part III of the Wrongs Act 1958" (the dependants' action for a wrongful death); "represented
-- person" (Guardianship and Administration Act 2019); the compensation schemes of s 27B(2) and s 40.
--
-- Dates use the built-in date functions only (no daydate). A period of n years "from" a day is reckoned without
-- that day (the reading of the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 (Vic) s 44, which is not deposited), so its
-- last day is the same day n years on; from 29 February, 28 February. READING, in NOTES.md (fork line 1).
--
-- BASELINE. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation of Actions Act 1958 (Vic) -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Dates`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`days after` `n` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is on or before` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is before` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `a` `b` MEANS IF `a` `is before` `b` THEN `b` ELSE `a`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` `a` `b` MEANS IF `a` `is before` `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- The number of days from a to b (negative if b is before a).
GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` `a` `to` `b` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `b` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `a`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `the year` IF
        ((`the year` MODULO 4) EQUALS 0 AND (NOT ((`the year` MODULO 100) EQUALS 0)))
    OR  (`the year` MODULO 400) EQUALS 0

GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER, `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of month` `the month` `the year` MEANS
    IF `the month` EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `is a leap year` `the year` THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF `the month` EQUALS 4 OR `the month` EQUALS 6 OR `the month` EQUALS 9 OR `the month` EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
         ELSE 31

-- The same date n months later; where that month is shorter, its last day.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` `n` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY
        (min (DATE_DAY `the day`) (`the last day of month` `the new month` `the new year`))
        `the new month`
        `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month index` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `the new month` MEANS (`the month index` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the new year` MEANS (`the month index` MINUS (`the month index` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12

-- The last day of a period of n years from a day: the same day n years on (29 February: 28 February).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of n years from` `n` `the day` MEANS `months after` (`n` TIMES 12) `the day`

-- The day a person born on a day turns a given age.
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER, `the birthday` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day of turning` `the age` `the birthday` MEANS `months after` (`the age` TIMES 12) `the birthday`

-- s 3(2) (line 50): "a person shall be deemed to be under a disability while he is a minor or of unsound mind".
-- Minor: under 18 (Age of Majority Act 1977, not deposited; asked nowhere, fixed here). s 3(3): a represented
-- person under the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 is conclusively of unsound mind (asked as a fact).
GIVEN `the birthday` IS A DATE, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `was a minor on` `the birthday` `the day` IF `the day` `is before` (`the day of turning` 18 `the birthday`)

GIVEN `the birthday` IS A DATE, `of unsound mind or a represented person` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(2) -- under a disability on` `the birthday` `of unsound mind or a represented person` `the day` IF
        `was a minor on` `the birthday` `the day`
    OR  `of unsound mind or a represented person`

§§ `Which limitation rule applies (s 4, s 5(9), s 23AB, s 27B, s 27N, ss 27O-27Q, s 40)`

-- The compensation schemes s 27B(2)(a)-(c) and s 40(a)-(c) (lines 548-550, 906-909) take out of Part IIA.
DECLARE `Compensation scheme` IS ONE OF
    `no compensation scheme`
    `Accident Compensation Act 1985 Part IV or Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 Part 7`
    `Workers Compensation Act 1958`
    `Transport Accident Act 1986 Part 6 or Part 10`

DECLARE `Kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `damages for my own personal injury`
    `a survivor action by the estate of a person who died`
    `a dependants' action for a death under Wrongs Act Part III`
    `contract or tort, not for death or personal injury and not defamation`
    `another kind of action`

-- The rule that sets the time limit. Each constructor names the section that sets it.
DECLARE `Limitation regime` IS ONE OF
    `no limitation period -- a worker's dust-related condition (s 23AB)`
    `no limitation period -- child abuse (s 27P)`
    `3 years from discoverability, no long-stop -- a dependants' action for a death from child abuse (s 27Q)`
    `Part IIA -- 3 or 6 years from discoverability or the 12-year long-stop, whichever ends first (ss 27D-27J)`
    `Part IIA, but no longer than the law before Part IIA -- act before 21 May 2003 (s 27N(4))`
    `the Act as in force before the 2002 amendments -- workplace or transport accident claim (s 40)`
    `Part I -- personal injury, 3 years (s 5(1AA), (1A))`
    `Part I -- contract or tort, 6 years (s 5(1)(a))`

-- s 23AB(1) (lines 425-430): no limitation period for damages for injury to a worker, brought by the worker or the
-- dependants of a deceased worker, where (a) the action is one to which Accident Compensation Act 1985 Part IV,
-- WIRC Act 2013 Part 7 or Wrongs Act 1958 Part III or VB applies and (b) the injury is a dust-related condition.
-- The estate (a survivor action) is not named: finding 2.
GIVEN `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim`
      `the injury is a dust-related condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injured person is a worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action comes under ACA Part IV, WIRC Act Part 7 or Wrongs Act Part III or VB` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23AB -- no limitation period for a worker's dust-related condition` IF
        `the injury is a dust-related condition`
    AND `the injured person is a worker`
    AND `the action comes under ACA Part IV, WIRC Act Part 7 or Wrongs Act Part III or VB`
    AND `brought by the worker or dependants`
    WHERE
        `brought by the worker or dependants` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of claim`
            WHEN `damages for my own personal injury` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a dependants' action for a death under Wrongs Act Part III` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 27O(1) (lines 684-688): Division 5 applies to an action in respect of a cause of action to which Part IIA applies
-- or extends, founded on death or personal injury resulting from physical or sexual abuse of the person as a minor
-- (and psychological abuse arising out of it).
--
-- The order of the tests:
--   1. Not death or personal injury: s 5(1)(a) for contract or tort; anything else is out (NOTHING).
--   2. s 23AB first: it applies "despite anything to the contrary in section 5 or section 40(a) and (b)" (s 23AB(2)),
--      and s 40 is "Subject to section 23AB".
--   3. s 27B(2)(a)-(c) with s 40: the workplace and transport accident schemes keep the Act as it stood before the
--      Limitation of Actions (Amendment) Act 2002 (not deposited).
--   4. s 27B(2)(d), (e): dust-related conditions and tobacco are outside Part IIA. For the injured person's own action
--      Part I s 5(1AA) or (1A) applies (s 5(9) does not exclude it). A survivor action or a Part III action outside
--      Part IIA takes its period from the Administration and Probate Act 1958 s 29 or the Wrongs Act 1958 s 20
--      (s 33, line 848), which are not here: NOTHING.
--   5. Division 5 (child abuse), which s 27N(6) puts before s 27N: s 27Q for a Part III action, s 27P otherwise.
--   6. s 27N(1), (2), (4): an act or omission before 21 May 2003 is under Part IIA, but Division 2 cannot make the
--      period longer than the law before Part IIA gave (that law is not deposited).
--   7. Otherwise Part IIA, Divisions 2 and 3.
-- s 27N(3) (proceedings commenced in a court before 1 October 2003) is out: it is not the seat's question.
GIVEN `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim`
      `the scheme` IS A `Compensation scheme`
      `the injury is a dust-related condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injured person is a worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action comes under ACA Part IV, WIRC Act Part 7 or Wrongs Act Part III or VB` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury results from tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury results from physical or sexual abuse as a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Limitation regime`
`the limitation regime` `the kind of claim` `the scheme` `the injury is a dust-related condition` `the injured person is a worker` `the action comes under ACA Part IV, WIRC Act Part 7 or Wrongs Act Part III or VB` `the injury results from tobacco` `the injury results from physical or sexual abuse as a minor` `the day of the act or omission` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of claim`
    WHEN `contract or tort, not for death or personal injury and not defamation` THEN
        JUST `Part I -- contract or tort, 6 years (s 5(1)(a))`
    WHEN `another kind of action` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF `s 23AB -- no limitation period for a worker's dust-related condition` `the kind of claim` `the injury is a dust-related condition` `the injured person is a worker` `the action comes under ACA Part IV, WIRC Act Part 7 or Wrongs Act Part III or VB`
        THEN JUST `no limitation period -- a worker's dust-related condition (s 23AB)`
        ELSE IF `s 27B(2)(a)-(c) -- a scheme excludes Part IIA` `the scheme`
             THEN JUST `the Act as in force before the 2002 amendments -- workplace or transport accident claim (s 40)`
             ELSE IF `the injury is a dust-related condition` OR `the injury results from tobacco`
                  THEN `outside Part IIA`
                  ELSE IF `the injury results from physical or sexual abuse as a minor`
                       THEN IF `a Part III action`
                            THEN JUST `3 years from discoverability, no long-stop -- a dependants' action for a death from child abuse (s 27Q)`
                            ELSE JUST `no limitation period -- child abuse (s 27P)`
                       ELSE IF `the day of the act or omission` `is before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 21 5 2003)
                            THEN JUST `Part IIA, but no longer than the law before Part IIA -- act before 21 May 2003 (s 27N(4))`
                            ELSE JUST `Part IIA -- 3 or 6 years from discoverability or the 12-year long-stop, whichever ends first (ss 27D-27J)`
    WHERE
        `a Part III action` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of claim`
            WHEN `a dependants' action for a death under Wrongs Act Part III` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `outside Part IIA` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind of claim`
            WHEN `damages for my own personal injury` THEN JUST `Part I -- personal injury, 3 years (s 5(1AA), (1A))`
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `the scheme` IS A `Compensation scheme`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27B(2)(a)-(c) -- a scheme excludes Part IIA` `the scheme` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the scheme`
    WHEN `no compensation scheme` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 27B(1), (2), (3) (lines 545-555): does Part IIA apply? JUST FALSE where s 27B(2) says "does not apply"; NOTHING
-- where the claim is not one for death or personal injury (s 27B(1) is a scope with no "only": rule (c)).
GIVEN `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim`
      `the scheme` IS A `Compensation scheme`
      `the injury is a dust-related condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury results from tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27B -- Part IIA applies` `the kind of claim` `the scheme` `the injury is a dust-related condition` `the injury results from tobacco` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of claim`
    WHEN `contract or tort, not for death or personal injury and not defamation` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `another kind of action` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF `s 27B(2)(a)-(c) -- a scheme excludes Part IIA` `the scheme`
            OR `the injury is a dust-related condition`
            OR `the injury results from tobacco`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part IIA Division 2 -- when a cause of action is discoverable (s 27F)`

-- s 27F(1), (2) (lines 582-586): discoverable on the first date the person knows or ought to have known (had they
-- taken all reasonable steps) all of: (a) the death or injury occurred; (b) it was caused by the defendant's fault;
-- (c) for personal injury, it was serious enough to justify an action. The first date all three are known is the
-- latest of the three dates. s 27F(4): a Part III action is not discoverable before the death.
GIVEN `the day the death or injury was known` IS A DATE
      `the day the defendant's fault was known` IS A DATE
      `the day the injury was known to be serious enough` IS A DATE
      `the claim is founded on a death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is a Part III action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 27F -- the day the cause of action is discoverable` `the day the death or injury was known` `the day the defendant's fault was known` `the day the injury was known to be serious enough` `the claim is founded on a death` `the claim is a Part III action` `the day of death` MEANS
    IF `the claim is a Part III action`
    THEN `the later of` `paragraphs (a) and (b)` `the day of death`
    ELSE IF `the claim is founded on a death`
         THEN `paragraphs (a) and (b)`
         ELSE `the later of` `paragraphs (a) and (b)` `the day the injury was known to be serious enough`
    WHERE
        `paragraphs (a) and (b)` MEANS `the later of` `the day the death or injury was known` `the day the defendant's fault was known`

§§ `Part IIA Division 2 -- legal incapacity (s 27J)`

-- s 27J(1), (4) (lines 613-628). A person is under a legal incapacity while (a) a minor not in the custody of a
-- capable parent or guardian, or (b) an incapacitated person for a continuous period of 28 days or more, but not
-- while a represented person whose guardian is authorised by law to bring actions in their name.
DECLARE `Kind of legal incapacity` IS ONE OF
    `no legal incapacity`
    `a minor not in the custody of a capable parent or guardian`
    `an incapacitated person without a guardian authorised to sue for them`

-- s 27J(2) (line 618): if the period "has commenced to run and the person is under a legal incapacity, the running of
-- the period of limitation is suspended for the duration of the legal incapacity". One spell of incapacity is taken.
-- The days suspended in a period that started on `the start` are the days of the spell on or after that start
-- (none if the spell ended before it, or began after the period's own last day). An incapacitated person's spell
-- counts only if it lasts 28 days or more (s 27J(1)(b)).
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of legal incapacity`
      `the spell began` IS A DATE
      `the spell ended` IS A DATE
      `the start` IS A DATE
      `the unsuspended last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 27J(2) -- the days suspended` `the kind` `the spell began` `the spell ended` `the start` `the unsuspended last day` MEANS
    IF `the spell counts`
        AND `the spell began` `is on or before` `the unsuspended last day`
        AND `the start` `is before` `the spell ended`
    THEN `days from` (`the later of` `the spell began` `the start`) `to` `the spell ended`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the spell counts` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the kind`
            WHEN `no legal incapacity` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `a minor not in the custody of a capable parent or guardian` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `an incapacitated person without a guardian authorised to sue for them` THEN
                (`days from` `the spell began` `to` `the spell ended`) AT LEAST 28

-- A period of n years from a start day, with s 27J suspension added.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER
      `the start` IS A DATE
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of legal incapacity`
      `the spell began` IS A DATE
      `the spell ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the period, with suspension` `n` `the start` `the kind` `the spell began` `the spell ended` MEANS
    `days after` (`s 27J(2) -- the days suspended` `the kind` `the spell began` `the spell ended` `the start` `the plain last day`) `the plain last day`
    WHERE
        `the plain last day` MEANS `the last day of n years from` `n` `the start`

§§ `Part IIA Division 2 -- the injured person's own action (ss 27D, 27E, 27I, 27J)`

-- s 27D(1) (lines 568-570): not after whichever ends first of (a) 3 years from discoverability and (b) 12 years from
-- the act or omission. s 27D(2), s 27E (lines 571-578): if the injured person was under a disability (s 3(2)) at
-- the act or omission, (a) becomes 6 years. s 27I(1) (lines 603-605): a minor injured by a parent or guardian or a
-- close associate of one: discoverable at the later of turning 25 and actual discoverability, and the long-stop is
-- 12 years from turning 25 (fork line 2: 27I(1)(b) replaces the 12-year limb of s 27D(1)(b) or s 27E(2)(b)).
-- s 27J suspends each period while the person is under a legal incapacity.
-- s 27N(4): for an act or omission before 21 May 2003 the earlier law may give a shorter period; it is not deposited,
-- so the answer is NOTHING.
GIVEN `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE
      `the day discoverable` IS A DATE
      `the injured person's birthday` IS A DATE
      `of unsound mind or a represented person at the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant was a parent or guardian or close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of legal incapacity` IS A `Kind of legal incapacity`
      `the spell began` IS A DATE
      `the spell ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ss 27D, 27E, 27I, 27J -- the last day for the injured person's action` `the day of the act or omission` `the day discoverable` `the injured person's birthday` `of unsound mind or a represented person at the act or omission` `the defendant was a parent or guardian or close associate of one` `the kind of legal incapacity` `the spell began` `the spell ended` MEANS
    IF `the day of the act or omission` `is before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 21 5 2003)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the earlier of` `the discoverability limb` `the long-stop limb`)
    WHERE
        `s 27I applies` MEANS
                `was a minor on` `the injured person's birthday` `the day of the act or omission`
            AND `the defendant was a parent or guardian or close associate of one`
        `the day of turning 25` MEANS `the day of turning` 25 `the injured person's birthday`
        `the deemed day discoverable` MEANS
            IF `s 27I applies`
            THEN `the later of` `the day of turning 25` `the day discoverable`
            ELSE `the day discoverable`
        `the long-stop start` MEANS
            IF `s 27I applies`
            THEN `the day of turning 25`
            ELSE `the day of the act or omission`
        `the years from discoverability` MEANS
            IF `s 3(2) -- under a disability on` `the injured person's birthday` `of unsound mind or a represented person at the act or omission` `the day of the act or omission`
            THEN 6
            ELSE 3
        `the discoverability limb` MEANS
            `the last day of the period, with suspension` `the years from discoverability` `the deemed day discoverable` `the kind of legal incapacity` `the spell began` `the spell ended`
        `the long-stop limb` MEANS
            `the last day of the period, with suspension` 12 `the long-stop start` `the kind of legal incapacity` `the spell began` `the spell ended`

§§ `Part IIA Division 2 -- survivor actions (s 27G, s 27I(3))`

-- s 27G (lines 592-595): for a survivor action the cause of action is deemed discoverable by the plaintiff (the
-- executor or administrator) at the earliest of (a) the day it was discoverable by the deceased, if that was more
-- than 3 years before the death; (b) the day of the plaintiff's appointment, if discoverable by the plaintiff at or
-- before it; (c) the day discoverable by the plaintiff, if after the appointment. (b) and (c) cannot both hold, and
-- one always does.
GIVEN `it was discoverable by the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day discoverable by the deceased` IS A DATE
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `the day of appointment` IS A DATE
      `the day discoverable by the plaintiff` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 27G -- the deemed day of discoverability for a survivor action` `it was discoverable by the deceased` `the day discoverable by the deceased` `the day of death` `the day of appointment` `the day discoverable by the plaintiff` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (a) applies`
    THEN `the earlier of` `the day discoverable by the deceased` `the day under paragraph (b) or (c)`
    ELSE `the day under paragraph (b) or (c)`
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) applies` MEANS
                `it was discoverable by the deceased`
            AND `the third anniversary of discoverability by the deceased` `is before` `the day of death`
        `the third anniversary of discoverability by the deceased` MEANS
            `the last day of n years from` 3 `the day discoverable by the deceased`
        `the day under paragraph (b) or (c)` MEANS
            IF `the day discoverable by the plaintiff` `is on or before` `the day of appointment`
            THEN `the day of appointment`
            ELSE `the day discoverable by the plaintiff`

-- The survivor action's last day. 3 or 6 years (s 27D(2), s 27E: the deceased's disability at the act or omission)
-- from the s 27G day, or 12 years from the act or omission, whichever ends first. s 27G is "Subject to section 27I":
-- where the deceased was a minor injured by a parent, guardian or close associate, the deemed day is the later of
-- turning 25 and the s 27G day, and the long-stop runs 12 years from turning 25; if the deceased died before turning
-- 25, the death takes the place of turning 25 (s 27I(3), line 609). Fork line 3. No s 27J suspension: the estate's
-- incapacity is not asked. Act or omission before 21 May 2003: NOTHING (s 27N(4)).
GIVEN `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE
      `the deceased's birthday` IS A DATE
      `the deceased was of unsound mind or a represented person at the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant was a parent or guardian or close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was discoverable by the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day discoverable by the deceased` IS A DATE
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `the day of appointment` IS A DATE
      `the day discoverable by the plaintiff` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ss 27D, 27E, 27G, 27I -- the last day for a survivor action` `the day of the act or omission` `the deceased's birthday` `the deceased was of unsound mind or a represented person at the act or omission` `the defendant was a parent or guardian or close associate of one` `it was discoverable by the deceased` `the day discoverable by the deceased` `the day of death` `the day of appointment` `the day discoverable by the plaintiff` MEANS
    IF `the day of the act or omission` `is before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 21 5 2003)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the earlier of` (`the last day of n years from` `the years from discoverability` `the deemed day`) (`the last day of n years from` 12 `the long-stop start`))
    WHERE
        `the s 27G day` MEANS `s 27G -- the deemed day of discoverability for a survivor action` `it was discoverable by the deceased` `the day discoverable by the deceased` `the day of death` `the day of appointment` `the day discoverable by the plaintiff`
        `s 27I applies` MEANS
                `was a minor on` `the deceased's birthday` `the day of the act or omission`
            AND `the defendant was a parent or guardian or close associate of one`
        `the day 27I counts from` MEANS
            `the earlier of` (`the day of turning` 25 `the deceased's birthday`) `the day of death`
        `the deemed day` MEANS
            IF `s 27I applies`
            THEN `the later of` `the day 27I counts from` `the s 27G day`
            ELSE `the s 27G day`
        `the long-stop start` MEANS
            IF `s 27I applies`
            THEN `the day 27I counts from`
            ELSE `the day of the act or omission`
        `the years from discoverability` MEANS
            IF `s 3(2) -- under a disability on` `the deceased's birthday` `the deceased was of unsound mind or a represented person at the act or omission` `the day of the act or omission`
            THEN 6
            ELSE 3

§§ `Part IIA -- the dependants' action for a death (s 27F(4), s 27H, s 27Q)`

-- s 27H (line 599): for a Part III action the long-stop runs from the date of death. s 27F(4): not discoverable before
-- the death. s 27D: 3 years (s 27E speaks of an action "founded on a personal injury", and a Part III action is
-- founded on the death: fork line 4). s 27Q (line 718): a Part III action within Division 5 (death from child abuse):
-- 3 years from discoverability, no long-stop; s 27N(6) keeps s 27N(4) away from it.
-- s 27I with a Part III action (a minor killed by a parent, guardian or close associate): s 27I(1)(b) would run the
-- long-stop from the victim's 25th birthday, which never comes, while s 27H runs it from the death; s 27I(3) settles
-- this only for a survivor action. NOTHING (finding 4).
GIVEN `the day of the act or omission` IS A DATE
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `the day discoverable` IS A DATE
      `the death resulted from physical or sexual abuse as a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased was a minor killed by a parent or guardian or close associate of one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ss 27D, 27F(4), 27H, 27Q -- the last day for a dependants' action for a death` `the day of the act or omission` `the day of death` `the day discoverable` `the death resulted from physical or sexual abuse as a minor` `the deceased was a minor killed by a parent or guardian or close associate of one` MEANS
    IF `the death resulted from physical or sexual abuse as a minor`
    THEN JUST (`the last day of n years from` 3 `the day not before death`)
    ELSE IF `the deceased was a minor killed by a parent or guardian or close associate of one`
            OR `the day of the act or omission` `is before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 21 5 2003)
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (`the earlier of` (`the last day of n years from` 3 `the day not before death`) (`the last day of n years from` 12 `the day of death`))
    WHERE
        `the day not before death` MEANS `the later of` `the day discoverable` `the day of death`

§§ `Part IIA Division 3 -- extension by the court (ss 27K-27M; s 23A outside Part IIA)`

-- s 27K(1) (line 635): a person claiming a cause of action under Part IIA may apply to a court to extend a Division 2
-- period; s 27M(1): at any time, even after the period expired or an action was commenced. s 27N(5): also for an act
-- before 21 May 2003. s 27O(4): Division 3 applies to a s 27Q action. s 27O(2): Divisions 2 and 3 "do not apply" to a
-- s 27P action (JUST FALSE). s 23A(2), (4), (6) (lines 404-421): outside Part IIA, an action for damages for
-- negligence, nuisance or breach of duty including personal injury may be extended by the court, at any time.
-- No power to extend a s 5(1)(a) contract or tort period for other loss (NOTHING: the Act is silent); s 23AB has no
-- period; s 40 keeps the earlier Act (not deposited): NOTHING.
GIVEN `the regime` IS A `Limitation regime`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 27K, 27M, 23A -- I may apply to a court to extend the period` `the regime` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the regime`
    WHEN `Part IIA -- 3 or 6 years from discoverability or the 12-year long-stop, whichever ends first (ss 27D-27J)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Part IIA, but no longer than the law before Part IIA -- act before 21 May 2003 (s 27N(4))` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `3 years from discoverability, no long-stop -- a dependants' action for a death from child abuse (s 27Q)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Part I -- personal injury, 3 years (s 5(1AA), (1A))` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `no limitation period -- child abuse (s 27P)` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 27K(2)(b), (3) (lines 638-639): if the court decides it is just and reasonable (having regard to the s 27L
-- matters), it may extend the period "for such period as the court determines", for an action brought by the
-- applicant in that court. The court's decision and the length are inputs; without an order the last day stays.
GIVEN `the last day before any extension` IS A DATE
      `the court orders an extension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days of extension ordered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 27K(3) -- the last day after an extension` `the last day before any extension` `the court orders an extension` `the days of extension ordered` MEANS
    IF `the court orders an extension`
    THEN `days after` `the days of extension ordered` `the last day before any extension`
    ELSE `the last day before any extension`

§§ `Part IIA Division 5 -- earlier judgments and settlements in child abuse claims (ss 27OA, 27QA-27QF, 27R, 27T)`

-- The window in s 27OA (previous judgment (b), previously settled cause of action (b)), s 27QA(1A) and s 27T: from 13
-- November 2024 to the commencement of the Justice Legislation Amendment (Vicarious Liability for Child Abuse) Act
-- 2026, 25 February 2026 (endnote, line 1212: "Ss 4-9 on 25.2.26"), both days in.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is in the 2024-2026 window` `the day` IF
        (DATE_FROM_DMY 13 11 2024) `is on or before` `the day`
    AND `the day` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 25 2 2026)

DECLARE `Earlier outcome` IS ONE OF
    `no earlier judgment or settlement`
    `dismissed as out of time, or an extension refused`
    `another judgment or order, including a dismissal`
    `settled by a settlement agreement`

-- s 27QA (lines 726-734): an action may be brought (1) on a previously barred cause of action (any limitation period
-- expired before 1 July 2015) even if dismissed as out of time or by refusing an extension; (1A) even if judgment or
-- an order (including dismissal) was given or made in the window; (2) on a previously settled cause of action
-- (settled before 1 July 2018, or in the window). (3): the section "does not apply" to a National Redress Scheme deed
-- of release or accepted offer, or a settlement taken into account in one: JUST FALSE. Outside its heads s 27QA is
-- silent (it grants, with no "only"): NOTHING. No earlier outcome: s 27QA is not needed (s 27P): NOTHING.
GIVEN `the earlier outcome` IS AN `Earlier outcome`
      `the day of the earlier outcome` IS A DATE
      `a limitation period expired before 1 July 2015` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a National Redress Scheme release or accepted offer covers it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27QA -- an action may be brought despite the earlier outcome` `the earlier outcome` `the day of the earlier outcome` `a limitation period expired before 1 July 2015` `a National Redress Scheme release or accepted offer covers it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the earlier outcome`
    WHEN `no earlier judgment or settlement` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF `a National Redress Scheme release or accepted offer covers it`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `a head applies` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `in the window` MEANS `is in the 2024-2026 window` `the day of the earlier outcome`
        `a head applies` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the earlier outcome`
            WHEN `dismissed as out of time, or an extension refused` THEN
                `a limitation period expired before 1 July 2015` OR `in the window`
            WHEN `another judgment or order, including a dismissal` THEN `in the window`
            WHEN `settled by a settlement agreement` THEN
                `the day of the earlier outcome` `is before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2018) OR `in the window`
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ss 27QB(3), 27QD(3), 27R(2), (3) (lines 741, 757, 786-788): a court other than the Supreme Court may not set aside a
-- judgment or order (or a settlement) of another court; the Supreme Court may set aside those of any court other
-- than the High Court. A settlement agreement given effect by no court order is "of" no court: any court hearing
-- the action may set it aside (fork line 5). ss 27QC(1), 27QE(1): only if the court is satisfied it is just and
-- reasonable (an input).
GIVEN `it was given effect by a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that court is the court hearing my action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that court was the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court hearing my action is the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 27QB, 27QD, 27R -- the court hearing the action has power to set it aside` `it was given effect by a court` `that court is the court hearing my action` `that court was the High Court` `the court hearing my action is the Supreme Court` IF
    IF NOT `it was given effect by a court`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `that court was the High Court`
         THEN FALSE
         ELSE `that court is the court hearing my action` OR `the court hearing my action is the Supreme Court`

-- s 27QF (lines 774-777): once a previous judgment or a settlement agreement is set aside, the person who paid under
-- it "is not entitled to seek to recover" the money on that basis (for a settlement, in accordance with the order;
-- a contract of insurance is not affected). JUST FALSE once set aside; NOTHING if nothing is set aside.
GIVEN `it has been set aside` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27QF -- the payer may recover what it paid` `it has been set aside` MEANS
    IF `it has been set aside` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- ss 27QC(2), 27QE(2) (lines 749-751, 764-770): in the new action the court may take into account amounts paid under a
-- judgment or settlement set aside, when awarding damages and costs, if satisfied it is just and reasonable.
GIVEN `it has been set aside` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied it is just and reasonable to take them into account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 27QC(2), 27QE(2) -- earlier payments may be taken into account` `it has been set aside` `the court is satisfied it is just and reasonable to take them into account` IF
    `it has been set aside` AND `the court is satisfied it is just and reasonable to take them into account`

DECLARE `What happened in the window` IS ONE OF
    `the claim was settled`
    `the claim was determined by a court, including by dismissal`
    `the claim was commenced and was still open on 25 February 2026`
    `none of these`

-- s 27T (lines 798-801): Division 5 as amended by No. 5/2026 applies to a cause of action that, in the window, was
-- settled, was determined by a court (including dismissal), or was commenced but not settled or determined before 25
-- February 2026. Outside those heads s 27T is silent (Division 5 otherwise applies by its own terms): NOTHING.
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened in the window`
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27T -- the 2026 amendments reach the cause of action` `what happened` `the day it happened` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what happened`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF `is in the 2024-2026 window` `the day it happened` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Part I with Part II -- outside Part IIA (ss 5, 23, 27)`

DECLARE `Part I action` IS ONE OF
    `contract or tort, other than personal injury`
    `personal injury`
    `personal injury that is a disease or disorder`

-- s 5(1)(a) (line 82): contract or tort, 6 years from accrual. s 5(1AA) (line 99): damages for personal injuries, 3
-- years from accrual. s 5(1A) (lines 101-103): a disease or disorder, 3 years from, and accrued on, the day the person
-- first knows (a) of the injury and (b) that it was caused by someone's act or omission (the "knowledge day").
-- s 27(1) (lines 515-519): fraud of the defendant, concealment by fraud, or relief from mistake: the period does not
-- begin until the fraud or mistake was or could with reasonable diligence have been discovered.
-- s 23(1) (lines 385-390): if the person was under a disability when the right accrued, the action may be brought
-- within 6 years of the day the disability ended or the person died, whichever came first, even after the period
-- expired. The "less number of years" proviso excepts s 5(1AA) and (1A), so 6 years applies to them too; proviso (a)
-- (the right first accrued to a person not under a disability through whom the claimant claims) removes the extension.
-- The last day is the later of the two.
GIVEN `the action` IS A `Part I action`
      `the day the cause of action accrued` IS A DATE
      `the knowledge day` IS A DATE
      `fraud or mistake postpones the start` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the fraud or mistake was or could have been discovered` IS A DATE
      `under a disability when it accrued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the disability ended or the person died` IS A DATE
      `the right first accrued to someone not under a disability through whom I claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`ss 5, 23, 27 -- the last day for a Part I action` `the action` `the day the cause of action accrued` `the knowledge day` `fraud or mistake postpones the start` `the day the fraud or mistake was or could have been discovered` `under a disability when it accrued` `the day the disability ended or the person died` `the right first accrued to someone not under a disability through whom I claim` MEANS
    IF `under a disability when it accrued`
        AND (NOT `the right first accrued to someone not under a disability through whom I claim`)
    THEN `the later of` `the plain last day` (`the last day of n years from` 6 `the day the disability ended or the person died`)
    ELSE `the plain last day`
    WHERE
        `the accrual` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the action`
            WHEN `personal injury that is a disease or disorder` THEN `the knowledge day`
            OTHERWISE `the day the cause of action accrued`
        `the start` MEANS
            IF `fraud or mistake postpones the start`
            THEN `the later of` `the accrual` `the day the fraud or mistake was or could have been discovered`
            ELSE `the accrual`
        `the years` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the action`
            WHEN `contract or tort, other than personal injury` THEN 6
            OTHERWISE 3
        `the plain last day` MEANS `the last day of n years from` `the years` `the start`

§§ `The bar as a rule`

DECLARE `Limitation party` IS ONE OF `the plaintiff`
DECLARE `Limitation action` IS ONE OF `bring the action`

-- "shall not be brought after the expiration of" the period (ss 5, 27D, 27E, 27Q). The plaintiff may bring the action
-- on any day up to and including the last day; once the period expires the action is barred. Counted in days from the
-- day the period starts (day 0), so an action brought on day n, where n is the days to the last day, is in time.
-- BREACH here means "the action is barred", not a wrong by the plaintiff: the Act states a bar, not a duty
-- (see NOTES.md, regulative rules).
GIVEN `the days to the last day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Limitation party` `Limitation action`
`the limitation bar` `the days to the last day` MEANS
    PARTY `the plaintiff`
    DO    `bring the action`
    WITHIN `the days to the last day`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the plaintiff` BECAUSE "the limitation period has expired and the action is barred"

-- The same test on dates: an action brought on a day is in time if that day is on or before the last day.
GIVEN `the day brought` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action is in time` `the day brought` `the last day` IF `the day brought` `is on or before` `the last day`
